#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198099 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "d40cb0df-fce7-5236-b0ef-62f5a343b3a3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12724" :question/problem "Consider the following compound predicates:\n\n$x$ is even **and** divisible by $5.$ \n\n$x$ is even **or** less than $6$.\n\nExpress these compound predicates above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is divisible by $5$\n\n- $C(x):$ $x$ is less than $6$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land.$\" \n\nSo, the first sentence reads\n\n![](images/6e/6e906074c9243c4189238c6ef5606954422bb7b8d2d3ad0b373579d25e221bb7.png)\n\nthat is, $A \\land B.$\n\nMoreover, the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor.$\" \n\nSo, the second sentence reads\n\n![](images/e5/e557113d18858d98a329fe4ce3ba84754defdc652095ccf57844077b7426d154.png)\n\nthat is, $A \\lor C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198100 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "3e2319b4-ab10-50ef-845b-9586c9761227" :question/math-academy-id "e-12725" :question/problem "Consider the following compound predicate:\n\n$x$ is positive **and** a multiple of $4,$ **or** $x$ is negative.\n\nExpress this compound predicate in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $M(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $4$\n\n- $N(x):$ $x$ is negative" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is positive and a multiple of $4.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x \\,\\textrm{is positive}}_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textrm{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{x \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a multiple of }4 }_M,\n$$\n\nthat is, $P \\land M.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is negative. This corresponds to $N.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x \\,\\textrm{ is positive}\\,\\textrm{and a multiple of }4 }_{P \\land M} \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textrm{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{x \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is negative} }_N,\n$$\n\nthat is, $(P \\land M) \\lor N.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198101 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198254 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6bc626a-9517-584c-bf55-8653227f830e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Sets of Conjunctions and Disjunctions"}] :question/id #uuid "3a115dd5-3241-5627-bb40-121b75eeb7ae" :question/math-academy-id "e-12726" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x) \\lor Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $\\mathbb{R}{:}$\n\n- $P(x):$ $3x -1 < 5$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x \\geq 3$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $P(x) \\lor Q(x)$ represents the *union* of the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x){:}$\n\n$$\nT_{P \\lor Q} = T_P \\cup T_Q\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x){:}$\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-1 & <5 \\\\ 3x & <6 \\\\ x & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n$T_P = (-\\infty,2).$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n$T_Q = [3,\\infty).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P∨Q} & ={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,2)\\cup [3,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198104 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198255 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f674fcf-7f3e-53c0-8759-6f83b0820160" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Conjunction and Disjunction"}] :question/id #uuid "2ab89571-f4e2-515f-9d01-b1213e73ffc0" :question/math-academy-id "e-12733" :question/problem "Write a sentence that is equivalent to the following: \"$x$ is an integer, and $x$ is negative and it is an integer.\"" :question/worked-solution "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"$x$ is negative and it is an integer\" with the phrase \"$x$ is an integer and it is negative.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is an integer, and $x$ is an integer and it is negative.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$x$ is an integer and $x$ is an integer, and it is negative.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$x$ is an integer and $x$ is an integer\" to just \"$x$ is an integer\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is an integer, and it is negative.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"$x$ is a negative integer.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822e6a30-0fa6-5438-9aa4-df4efa9a1785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194761} {:answer/id #uuid "92f13186-7ef2-56a6-afaa-ede0ce2ed159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194762} {:answer/id #uuid "9cab27f4-f8c8-5435-ac8b-25cb574b6b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194763} {:answer/id #uuid "b2a7869d-8b6d-53eb-b4a4-fc00d63915d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194764} {:answer/id #uuid "629b3ce3-6280-547d-8a34-4dc84203c7a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194765}] :answer-field/id #uuid "bb53ef75-3c2a-5730-a062-a4208ae377f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41dde3e3-6092-50d7-a3e3-9b03129714b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381363} {:answer/id #uuid "ab38e2e3-7aa0-5681-bd79-b716a1f5ebfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381364} {:answer/id #uuid "765bffbf-d84a-5ff5-a5f8-870a92ad58fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381365} {:answer/id #uuid "63cf5e8f-593a-5960-b49a-27fd32e7eff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381366} {:answer/id #uuid "1b83a791-8241-5cd5-855b-476449665c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b83a791-8241-5cd5-855b-476449665c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381367} :answer-field/id #uuid "b22e7a73-f4cf-5a91-83ba-e94d101da87b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ff7b2b7-dfb5-55b1-bfd4-172f42c8239c" :question/math-academy-id "q-170725" :question/problem "$x$ is even **or** odd.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is odd" :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "443c2ac2-d73e-5209-b21f-beb333bf7d18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨(A∧B)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381370} {:answer/id #uuid "ea606823-2fa9-5cc2-990c-5045edd76dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381371} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7ab119-0282-5fbe-9bf9-0e338586bd6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧(B∨A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381372} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3b63ed-53f9-5121-b506-5b94b2f06ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381373} {:answer/id #uuid "baa4f7d6-0324-5b7e-8071-793d1a8bec13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B∧B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea606823-2fa9-5cc2-990c-5045edd76dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381371} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc686a5e-3a2b-5cc8-ad6d-1246bf1f5079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "694a195b-decb-5476-962c-92767f80b122" :question/math-academy-id "q-170735" :question/problem "$x$ is rational  **or** greater than $10.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is rational\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is greater than $10$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x>10}_{⏟}}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∨B.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d99eb173-3abf-5775-a859-5a92ae2ae01f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨R)∨(P∨I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381504} {:answer/id #uuid "df7b7424-fa58-5870-87bc-c682e2678be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨R)∧(P∨I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381505} {:answer/id #uuid "28e544d4-09ee-5450-aac7-cedff79d4967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((N∨R)∧P)∨I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381506} {:answer/id #uuid "d99f5091-2095-5600-a488-bf4114dc1018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∧R)∧(P∧I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381507} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd81fe8-96cc-5534-bfef-3c16765feb7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∧R)∨(P∧I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df7b7424-fa58-5870-87bc-c682e2678be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨R)∧(P∨I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381505} :answer-field/id #uuid "33ea1fa2-4f60-58ac-aee0-0a9d809fa209" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "357fd90c-bc44-5b21-9839-d55874391b78" :question/math-academy-id "q-175377" :question/problem "$x$ is negative **or** rational, **and** $x$ is positive **or** an  integer.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $N(x):$ $x$ is negative\n\n- $R(x):$ $x$ is rational\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $I(x):$ $x$ is an integer" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$,\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is negative **or** rational. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is negative }}_{⏟}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is rational }}_{⏟}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∨R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is positive **or** an integer. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is positive }}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is an integer }}_{⏟}}_{I},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨I.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is negative or rational}}_{⏟}}_{N\\,∨\\,R}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\text{ is positive or an integer }}_{⏟}}_{P\\,∨\\,I},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(N∨R)∧(P∨I).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198254 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6bc626a-9517-584c-bf55-8653227f830e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Sets of Conjunctions and Disjunctions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ec4788-c9fa-5856-aa79-ed932a7b324d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9fc6aa4f7f220a14f33ed6269d598dd7aae24f6efac4caf80c8e7f5386450a5a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389792} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc1c924-ac4a-5694-9ff3-76277fe7d08c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/78/781bd7c0c99aa965c5b20b6545e1ab76acbbc88d7698fbed1afe3e7a6d22a14c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389793} {:answer/id #uuid "ef857f1a-d365-55c1-9f94-4a0e4c46efc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1a/1ab3b9c6a9a4b9f7bb4c481770e9fbf2beec8998eda65d22418535dca31d58bc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389794} {:answer/id #uuid "88e6a03c-020e-515c-97ad-a0dbc44a2bc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ef/efa51ca7fcb2e24c5f7a77114a7accb008696dd012d60307937c26c1039e6892.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389795} {:answer/id #uuid "8944f4c5-55a9-51e1-a1e9-7dc77668ffb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/de4621c16bad151116f6c6fa4b197c6207b527bff90e5f9c857405ca3e6b135d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20ec4788-c9fa-5856-aa79-ed932a7b324d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9fc6aa4f7f220a14f33ed6269d598dd7aae24f6efac4caf80c8e7f5386450a5a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389792} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d9db75d-b8b1-5171-a35a-f70bc057c59e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4eda50f7-a585-5a86-9e62-dbc7c5c300f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-177645" :question/problem "![](images/76/761e02a7613e2d1df4722b7bf6f0a7e1d0b5e7b6dec09d205a1e72a29b8c5eb8.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of the predicates $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P∨Q?$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $P∨Q$ represents the *union* of the truth sets of $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∨Q}={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $P(x,y)∨Q(x,y),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}$ or ${T}_{Q},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/9f/9fc6aa4f7f220a14f33ed6269d598dd7aae24f6efac4caf80c8e7f5386450a5a.png)\n\n**Note:** The points where the *solid* line meets the *dashed* curve belong to ${T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}$ since these points lie in ${T}_{P}.$"}]}
